Would you mind to elaborate why a lock would also be needed to read a sys.flags flag?

`sys.flags` is a `structseq` instance which inherits from `tuple`. Getting a tuple item doesn't use any lock:

```c
static PyObject *
tuple_item(PyObject *op, Py_ssize_t i)
{
    PyTupleObject *a = _PyTuple_CAST(op);
