If we add things to the bind data, they must also be serialized, otherwise logical plans are not round-trippable. We need to be careful when adding new serialization, because we need these plans to stay roundtrippable (we can't just go back on our decisions after a release and invalidate old plans, but we could ignore fields if we want). So, I'd say we need to be careful with adding things here. It also seems very specific to length pushdown, which is not generic/extensible in the future.

