I've ran it through the MacOS instruments profiler, and ~25% of the time spent is in this loop. I think it can be optimized significantly. We might even be able to create a branchless loop.

For example, you can check `validity_mask.AllValid()` before the loop, and remove the check `validity_mask.RowIsValid(i)` from the loop (of course, this means you need to implement the loop twice, or template it).

I would also just cast `src` to a `bool *`, then you don't need to check if it's 0 or 1. In debug mode, it will automatically throw if it loads something that's not a 0 or 1. This removes another branch from the loop.

