Let's put this into a method on localStreamLimits, so we keep all the locking in one place.

Let's also add an unlock method to localStreamLimits, so we have only one copy of the gate-state-setting logic:

```
// wasOpened reports whether the given stream was opened by us.
func (lim *localStreamLimits) wasOpened(num int64) bool {
  lim.gate.lock()
  defer lim.unlock()
  return num < lim.opened
}

func (lim *localStreamLimits) unlock() {
  lim.gate.Unlock(lim.opened < lim.max)
}
